g  role and who's not and remember for  prince philip's funeral the queen made  the decision everyone should wear suits  everyone's on a laying plane level  playing field this is different but who  does this decision come from this edict  come from it comes from the king right  it comes from the kingdom it's a  decision that the king has taken well  why would they do that i mean then the  press here and the tabloid press will  make this big deal about prince harry  being in a suit but he made his own  decision to step back from royal duties  i think the view that the king has taken  is that there is a difference between  the funeral of the consort prince philip  and a state occasion this is the first  state funeral of harmonix since 1952  this is massive and so he wants to get  everything absolutely technically right  and it's only technically right that  only working members of the royal family  wear military uniform harry is no longer  a working member of the royal family but  that will be painful to him because of  course he served in afghanistan he  served he has done an enormous amount of  military duty 10 years of service  i want to bring in gail king who i know  will have additional questions on the  scale  i do roy roy anika it's good to see you  and you're right i think that will be  very painful to harry you know the other  day when king charles extended  when he expressed love for megan and  harry many people are speculating that  he was extending an olive branch i know  you've covered the royals for years  you've gotten to know them  so based on what you know did you see it  as an olive branch as well  well good morning gail i have to say i  have seen the last few days as nothing  but olive branches from the new king and  indeed the new prince of wales it was  really significant as you say that he  mentioned harry and megan in that  address  the next day when he signed his  proclamations at the accession council  he was using a silver ink pot that  william and harry had jointly given to  him these are really important symbols  and of course we know you know he is  he's going out of his way to make sure  they're included  that that moment from william reaching  out to harry as well on saturday saying  please come and come with us to windsor  and let's see do this walk about  together these are all really important  olive branches that are being extended  to harry and megan and they're being  welcomed which is crucial as well  he's also talked about slimming down the  royal family the working royal family  what does that look like what exactly  does that mean  do you know i think that's really  interesting i think we have seen that  shedding of members of the royal family  just by sort of natural wastage almost  in the last couple of years harry and  megan have stepped back andrew has  stepped back but i think going forwards  when you talk about the streamlined  monarchy it's just what nora was talking  about the weight of responsibility on  william and kate now be enormous you  know the focus over the next few days is  going to be this is the future it's very  tight it's william kate and and and  charles siblings and that's it  all right we have to go roy but i did  have one question about him being called  the prince of wales why was that  necessary what does that mean that now  charles that now william and kate are  the prince and princess of wales  you know what it wasn't naturally  automatically going to happen that was  decision from the king i think it's  really important that it shows that  william is following in the footsteps of  his father and it's it's a sign here  recognition of his seniority that he is  a heartbeat away from being king that's  what that title means  all right roy anika i knew you would  have the information we thank you we  thank you norah always good to see you  thanks a lot

